{"nodes":[{"id":"9f26f662240e01fd","type":"text","text":"Recurrent\n\n循环的","x":50,"y":50,"width":260,"height":120},{"id":"bccfdc96d9631503","type":"text","text":"convolutional\n\n卷积","x":330,"y":50,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"4"},{"id":"443796679c7c1f77","type":"text","text":"self-respect\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: A feeling of pride and confidence in oneself; a sense of one’s own worth or value.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 自尊  \n4) **Example sentence**: Most of us strive for self-respect — to see ourselves in a positive light, to be proud of who we are.","x":610,"y":50,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"4"},{"id":"85ac05e21491746c","type":"text","text":"undermine\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Verb  \n2) **English definition**: To weaken or damage something, especially someone’s confidence, authority, or feelings, often gradually or insidiously.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 削弱；损害；暗中破坏  \n4) **Example sentence**: Any comments or experiences that undermine those feelings of self-worth can be uncomfortable.","x":50,"y":190,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"1"},{"id":"45aa5cd8bc91fc10","type":"text","text":"perception\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: The way in which something is regarded, understood, or interpreted, often based on sensory experience or mental awareness.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 感知；认知；看法  \n4) **Example sentence**: \"Perception D.\" (The original sentence is incomplete, but a full example: \"Her perception of the situation changed after learning the truth.\")","x":330,"y":190,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"49a5cc4526688794","type":"text","text":"citation\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: A reference to a source (such as a book, article, or legal case) that provides authority or evidence for a statement or claim.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 引用；引证  \n4) **Example sentence**: *Citation B* refers to the second source listed in the bibliography.","x":610,"y":190,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"1"},{"id":"b6859ac9f45b5928","type":"text","text":"imitation\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: The act of copying or reproducing something, often as a less authentic or inferior version.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 模仿；仿制品  \n4) **Example sentence**: *imitation C.* (This suggests \"imitation\" is used as a label or category, likely meaning a copy or replica of type C.)","x":50,"y":330,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"1"},{"id":"085b47fec20196fe","type":"text","text":"foolish\n\n1) Part of speech: Adjective  \n2) English definition: Lacking good sense, judgment, or wisdom; unwise.  \n3) Chinese translation: 愚蠢的；不明智的  \n4) Example sentence: It was foolish of him to go out in the rain without an umbrella.","x":330,"y":330,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"fc06e4b1b1ab9ca7","type":"text","text":"interpreting\n\n1) **Part of speech:** Verb (gerund/present participle)  \n2) **Chinese translation:** 解读 / 诠释  \n3) **Example sentence:** She kept interpreting his silence as a sign of disapproval.","x":610,"y":330,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"4"},{"id":"8966ac0e444ac23b","type":"text","text":"term\n\n1) Part of speech: noun  \n2) Chinese translation: 术语；说法  \n3) Example sentence: The term for this way of thinking is personalisation.","x":50,"y":470,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"d6094b883bfc9411","type":"text","text":"quotations\n\nBased on the context provided (the fragment \"quotations B\"), here is the definition:\n\n1) **Part of speech:** Noun (plural)\n2) **Chinese translation:** 引用/报价 (bàojià) — specifically referring to price quotes or estimates in a business or financial context.\n3) **Example sentence:** \"Please send us your latest quotations for product B.\"","x":330,"y":470,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"ce70f6230dd761f2","type":"text","x":610,"y":470,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"at work\n\n短语，起作用","color":"2"},{"id":"d0c17ed99dd591f4","type":"text","x":50,"y":610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"accounting for\n\nBased on the context provided (which appears to be a fragment, likely from a sentence like \"X is responsible for accounting for C\"), here is the definition:\n\n1)  **Part of speech:** Phrasal verb (prepositional verb)\n2)  **Detailed Chinese translation:** 解释；说明；占（比例）；对…负责\n3)  **Example sentence for each meaning:**\n    *   **Meaning 1 (To explain or give a reason):** The manager had to **account for** the missing funds. (经理必须**解释**资金丢失的原因。)\n    *   **Meaning 2 (To constitute a specified portion):** The service sector **accounts for** over 60% of the country's GDP. (服务业**占**该国GDP的60%以上。)\n    *   **Meaning 3 (To be responsible for):** Each employee is **accounting for** their own time sheet. (每位员工都要**对**自己的考勤表**负责**。)","color":"2"},{"id":"213bb1a50c576684","type":"text","x":330,"y":610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"interfering with\n\nBased on the context provided (only the phrase \"interfering with\"), here is the definition:\n\n1)  **Part of speech:** Verb phrase (present participle of \"interfere with\")\n2)  **Detailed Chinese translation:** 干涉；妨碍；干扰；介入（并阻碍）\n3)  **Example sentence for each meaning:**\n    *   **干涉 (to meddle):** Stop **interfering with** my personal life.\n    *   **妨碍 (to hinder/obstruct):** The storm is **interfering with** our travel plans.\n    *   **干扰 (to disrupt):** Please don't **interfere with** the machine while it's running.","color":"1"},{"id":"65c6c288b4191468","type":"text","x":610,"y":610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"interpretations\n\nHere is the concise definition for \"interpretations\" based on the provided context:\n\n1) **All meanings for the word:**\n   - The action of explaining or understanding the meaning of something.\n   - A particular way of performing or presenting something (e.g., a piece of art or music).\n\n2) **Chinese translation for each meaning:**\n   - 解释；理解；解读\n   - 演绎；表演方式\n\n3) **Example sentence (using the original sentence):**\n   - \"When you find yourself taking a situation personally, try to think of other **interpretations** that are less focused on you — especially in the sense of saying anything deep or __(17)__ about you.\""},{"id":"2f692edf52dc2e8d","type":"text","x":50,"y":750,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"feedback\n\nBased on the context provided (the sentence \"feedback C.\"), the word \"feedback\" is likely being used in a technical or systematic sense, possibly as a label or category. Here is the definition:\n\n**Feedback**  \n1) **Meaning**: Information about reactions to a product, a person's performance of a task, etc., used as a basis for improvement; or the return of a portion of the output of a system to the input, especially in electronics or cybernetics.  \n2) **Chinese translation**: 反馈；回馈  \n3) **Example sentence**: *The system uses feedback to adjust its output.* (The original sentence \"feedback C.\" is too brief to serve as a full example, but it suggests a category or label, e.g., \"Feedback C\" as a type of feedback.)","color":"2"},{"id":"04d86d117e682750","type":"text","x":330,"y":750,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"nnovate\n\nBased on the context provided, here is the definition:\n\n1) **Meaning**: To introduce something new; to make changes in something established, especially by introducing new methods, ideas, or products. (Note: \"nnovate\" appears to be a typo for \"innovate.\")\n2) **Chinese translation**: 创新；革新\n3) **Example sentence**: innovate B. (This sentence is incomplete, but it suggests applying innovation to \"B,\" which could represent a product, process, or field.)","color":"2"},{"id":"f79b2b9a68892cd8","type":"text","x":610,"y":750,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"springs to mind\n\n浮现在脑海中","color":"2"},{"id":"ea432611da8eca57","type":"text","x":50,"y":890,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"dusty\n\n布满灰尘的","color":"4"},{"id":"b300b618ac36a387","type":"text","x":330,"y":890,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"rather like\n\n和...颇为相像","color":"4"},{"id":"56fd3000cb777a2d","type":"text","x":610,"y":890,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"startlingly\n\n惊人地","color":"4"},{"id":"7fa7536cf331dc4c","type":"text","x":50,"y":1030,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"commissioned\n\n受委托","color":"4"},{"id":"7cd5843e1f841a6f","type":"text","x":330,"y":1030,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"branches\n\n树枝\n分支，这里指分店","color":"4"},{"id":"e013898d6d93996d","type":"text","x":610,"y":1030,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"hive\n\n蜂巢\nzh-CN"},{"id":"9a3402282efcb6ce","type":"text","x":50,"y":1170,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"multitude\n\n众多\nzh-CN","color":"2"},{"id":"2085bd28a85f0a51","type":"text","x":330,"y":1170,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"entrepreneurs\n\n企业家\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"492ecde1bceb106d","type":"text","x":610,"y":1170,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"justify\n\n辩解\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"9fa300fda9df541c","type":"text","x":50,"y":1310,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"overlooked\n\n被忽视\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"eb37f5f95fe5a332","type":"text","x":330,"y":1310,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"underappreciated\n\n被低估\nzh-CN","color":"2"},{"id":"81886f7e5a4c8332","type":"text","x":610,"y":1310,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"impose\n\n强加\nzh-CN","color":"2"},{"id":"b87547bf4e8e4ba8","type":"text","x":50,"y":1450,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"disputed\n\n有争议\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"32b3cea52608c794","type":"text","x":330,"y":1450,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"flaws\n\n缺陷\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"e55aa437c699da8d","type":"text","x":610,"y":1450,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"campaign\n\n活动\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"57317b465bb21089","type":"text","x":50,"y":1590,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"memberships\n\n会员资格\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"1b58c1049ed74755","type":"text","x":330,"y":1590,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"confidential\n\n保密\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"b6a6ac8e72154a0f","type":"text","x":610,"y":1590,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"facilitate\n\n方便\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"d2ade82cb99127b1","type":"text","x":50,"y":1730,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"cited\n\n引用\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"424b7e8ea369ce9c","type":"text","x":330,"y":1730,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"outright\n\n直接\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"d30bf0c20d5e2b92","type":"text","x":610,"y":1730,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"landscape\n\n景观、格局\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"eb75d8b1507c0a30","type":"text","x":50,"y":1870,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"leveraging\n\n利用\nzh-CN","color":"2"},{"id":"4dfb540b97685472","type":"text","x":330,"y":1870,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"retains\n\n保留\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"d6e944bc20011934","type":"text","x":610,"y":1870,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"transparency\n\n透明度\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"7655fc88bf37aa6b","type":"text","x":50,"y":2010,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"navigate\n\n导航\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"bae81edce4fd2897","type":"text","x":330,"y":2010,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"cautiously\n\n谨慎\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"6cbeb858d03c5931","type":"text","x":610,"y":2010,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"budgets\n\n预算\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"53391c933355afa1","type":"text","x":50,"y":2150,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"overemphasise\n\n过分强调","color":"3"},{"id":"0da160768e66e294","type":"text","x":330,"y":2150,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"excessively\n\n过度\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"9c335d569c2f8e3c","type":"text","x":610,"y":2150,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"terms\n\nterms\n<i:100>\n[ielts]\n\nn. 条件, 条款, 费用, 价钱, 关系, 地位, 交谊\n[经] 条件\n\n释义: n status with respect to the relations between people or groups\nn the amount of money needed to purchase something\nn a word or expression used for some particular thing\nn a limited period of time\nn (usually plural) a statement of what is required as part of an agreement\nn any distinct quantity contained in a polynomial\nn one of the substantive phrases in a logical proposition\nn the end of gestation or point at which birth is imminent\nn (architecture) a statue or a human bust or an animal carved out of the top of a square pillar; originally used as a boundary marker in ancient Rome\nv name formally or designate with a term","color":"3"},{"id":"00424ecc912b227d","type":"text","x":50,"y":2290,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"chaos\n\nchaos\n/'keiɒs/\n<n:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 大混乱, 混沌\n[化] 混沌; 浑沌\n\n释义: n. a state of extreme confusion and disorder\nn. the formless and disordered state of matter before the creation of the cosmos\nn. (Greek mythology) the most ancient of gods; the personification of the infinity of space preceding creation of the universe\nn. (physics) a dynamical system that is extremely sensitive to its initial conditions","color":"3"},{"id":"bf0b2b6f88eb0823","type":"text","x":330,"y":2290,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"Disruptions\n\ndisruptions\n/disˈrʌpʃənz/\n\nn. 中断( disruption的复数形式 ); 分裂; 瓦解; 破坏\n\n释义: n. an act of delaying or interrupting the continuity\nn. a disorderly outburst or tumult\nn. an event that results in a displacement or discontinuity","color":"4"},{"id":"5065ef2d6eca105b","type":"text","x":610,"y":2290,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"meantime\n\nmeantime\n/'mi:ntaim/\n<r:1/n:99>\n[cet4 cet6 ky]\n\nn. 间隔时间, 其时\nadv. 其间\n\n释义: n the time between one event, process, or period and another\nr during the intervening time","color":"3"},{"id":"8a397a91ec168145","type":"text","x":50,"y":2430,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"congestion\n\ncongestion\n/kәn'dʒestʃәn/\n<n:100>\n[toefl ielts]\n\nn. 拥挤, 充血\n[计] 拥挤, 拥塞\n\n释义: n. excessive accumulation of blood or other fluid in a body part\nn. excessive crowding","color":"1"},{"id":"2a815df6da59801a","type":"text","x":330,"y":2430,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"segregation\n\nsegregation\n/.segri'geiʃәn/\n<n:100>\n\nn. 隔离, 偏析, 被隔离的部分, 种族隔离\n[化] 分离; 分凝; 离析; 偏析; 分聚\n\n释义: n. (genetics) the separation of paired alleles during meiosis so that members of each pair of alleles appear in different gametes\nn. a social system that provides separate facilities for minority groups\nn. the act of segregating or sequestering","color":"1"},{"id":"681ca202b8263799","type":"text","x":610,"y":2430,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"density\n\ndensity\n/'densiti/\n<n:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nn. 密度\n[化] 密度\n\n释义: n. the amount per unit size","color":"3"},{"id":"c4e9e8ecbf3bd3f3","type":"text","x":50,"y":2570,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"reduction\n\nreduction\n/ri'dʌkʃәn/\n<n:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nn. 减少, 缩影, 变化\n[化] 还原\n\n释义: n. any process in which electrons are added to an atom or ion (as by removing oxygen or adding hydrogen); always occurs accompanied by oxidation of the reducing agent\nn. the act of reducing complexity","color":"3"},{"id":"dd9b44af0d814cc2","type":"text","x":330,"y":2570,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"fluidity\n\nfluidity\n/flu:'iditi/\n<n:100>\n\nn. 流动性, 流质, 流状\n[化] 流动性; 流度\n\n释义: n. the property of flowing easily\nn. a changeable quality","color":"3"},{"id":"af785ee5bc8129bc","type":"text","x":610,"y":2570,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"intervals\n\nintervals\n/'ɪntevl/\n\nn. [军事]间隔( interval的复数形式 ); 间隔时间; [数学]区间; （戏剧、电影或音乐会的）幕间休息\n\n释义: n. a definite length of time marked off by two instants\nn. a set containing all points (or all real numbers) between two given endpoints\nn. the distance between things","color":"3"},{"id":"748f520e7e086b65","type":"text","x":50,"y":2710,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"beloved\n\nbeloved\n/bi'lʌvd/\n<j:94/n:6>\n[cet4 ky ielts]\n\na. 心爱的\nn. 心爱的人\n\n释义: n. a beloved person; used as terms of endearment\ns. dearly loved","color":"3"},{"id":"2794b0f01e9134ed","type":"text","x":330,"y":2710,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"stage\n\nstage\n/steidʒ/\n<v:8/n:92>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky ielts]\n\nn. 阶段, 舞台, 场所, 戏剧, 站, 驿站, 级, 层, 脚手架\nvt. 上演, 表演, 筹划\nvi. 适于上演, 乘驿车旅行\n\n释义: n. a large platform on which people can stand and can be seen by an audience\nn. the theater as a profession (usually `the stage')\nn. a section or portion of a journey or course\nn. any scene regarded as a setting for exhibiting or doing something","color":"3"},{"id":"44ee207fec1a0b35","type":"text","x":610,"y":2710,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"blossomed\n\nblossomed\n/ˈblɔsəmd/\n\nv. （植物）开花( blossom的过去式和过去分词 ); 发展; 长成; 变得更加健康（或自信、成功）\n\n释义: imp. & p. p. of Blossom","color":"3"},{"id":"28fbb22cd7337039","type":"text","x":50,"y":2850,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"abruptly\n\nabruptly\n/ә'brʌptli/\n<r:100>\n\nadv. 突然地, 唐突地\n\n释义: r. quickly and without warning","color":"3"},{"id":"8ede0102ca8f35f4","type":"text","x":330,"y":2850,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"primary\n\nprimary\n/'praimәri/\n<j:76/n:24>\n[zk gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 最主要者, 原色\na. 主要的, 初期的, 根本的, 原始的, 首要的, 基本的\n[计] 初等量; 主要的; 一次的\n\n释义: n. a preliminary election where delegates or nominees are chosen\nn. one of the main flight feathers projecting along the outer edge of a bird's wing\nn. (astronomy) a celestial body (especially a star) relative to other objects in orbit around it\na. of first rank or importance or value; direct and immediate rather than secondary","color":"4"},{"id":"a4ff4dfed28874d8","type":"text","x":610,"y":2850,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"skyrocketed\n\nskyrocketed\n/ˈskaɪˌrɔkɪtid/\n\nv. 突升, 猛涨( skyrocket的过去式和过去分词 )\n\n释义: v shoot up abruptly, like a rocket","color":"3"},{"id":"4196716ddd53f3b7","type":"text","x":50,"y":2990,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"entertainment\n\nentertainment\n/.entә'teinmәnt/\n<n:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 娱乐, 款待, 娱乐表演\n\n释义: n. an activity that is diverting and that holds the attention","color":"4"},{"id":"7e134c51bbb8a404","type":"text","x":330,"y":2990,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"portable\n\nportable\n/'pɒ:tәbl/\n<j:94/n:6>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 可携带的, 可搬运的, 可移动的\n[计] 可移植的\n\n释义: n. a small light typewriter; usually with a case in which it can be carried\na. easily or conveniently transported\ns. of a motor designed to be attached to the outside of a boat's hull","color":"1"},{"id":"16c7c37439962605","type":"text","x":610,"y":2990,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"fencing\n\nfencing\n/'fensiŋ/\n<n:100>\n[toefl gre]\n\nn. 围墙, 剑术\n[法] 围栏, 买卖赃物, 辩论\n\n释义: n. the art or sport of fighting with swords (especially the use of foils or epees or sabres to score points under a set of rules)","color":"1"},{"id":"29d18de24b0af833","type":"text","x":50,"y":3130,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"facilities\n\nfacilities\n[ielts gre]\n\nn. 工具, 设施, 设备\n\n释义: n a building or place that provides a particular service or is used for a particular industry\nn skillful performance or ability without difficulty\nn a natural effortlessness\nn something designed and created to serve a particular function and to afford a particular convenience or service\nn a service that an organization or a piece of equipment offers you","color":"1"},{"id":"2daa8e5018c2c580","type":"text","x":330,"y":3130,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"relieve\n\nrelieve\n/ri'li:v/\n<v:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nvt. 减轻, 救济, 解除, 使免除, 换...的班, 使得到调剂, 使不单调, 衬托, 使显著\nvi. 救济, 当替补投手, 呈鲜明突出\n\n释义: v. provide physical relief, as from pain\nv. free from a burden, evil, or distress\nv. take by stealing\nv. alleviate or remove (pressure or stress) or make less oppressive","color":"1"},{"id":"d7649c47f5d58e66","type":"text","x":610,"y":3130,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"foster\n\nfoster\n/'fɒstә/\n<j:45/v:55>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 收养的, 养育的\nvt. 养育, 抚育, 培养, 鼓励, 抱(希望)\n\n释义: n. United States songwriter whose songs embody the sentiment of the South before the American Civil War (1826-1864)\nv. promote the growth of\nv. bring up under fosterage; of children\nv. help develop, help grow","color":"1"},{"id":"0e9b5610a4a0b1d5","type":"text","x":50,"y":3270,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"vibrancy\n\nvibrancy\n/'vaibrәnsi/\n<n:100>\n[gre]\n\nn. 振动, 振响, 活力\n\n释义: n having the character of a loud deep sound; the quality of being resonant","color":"1"},{"id":"37cf3de6c65db137","type":"text","x":330,"y":3270,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"amateur\n\namateur\n/'æmәtә/\n<j:61/n:39>\n[gk cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 业余爱好者, 外行, 爱好者\n[电] 业余家\n\n释义: n. someone who pursues a study or sport as a pastime\nn. an athlete who does not play for pay\ns. engaged in as a pastime","color":"1"},{"id":"7b22688e612e3af7","type":"text","x":610,"y":3270,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"prominent\n\nprominent\n/'prɒminәnt/\n<j:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 卓越的, 显著的, 突出的, 凸出的\n\n释义: s having a quality that thrusts itself into attention\ns conspicuous in position or importance","color":"1"},{"id":"56ecf3a69c24dc90","type":"text","x":50,"y":3410,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"generosity\n\ngenerosity\n/.dʒenә'rɒsiti/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 gre]\n\nn. 慷慨, 宽大\n\n释义: n. the trait of being willing to give your money or time\nn. acting generously","color":"1"},{"id":"52550ea33edddccc","type":"text","x":330,"y":3410,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"expenditures\n\nexpenditures\n/ɪks'pendɪtʃəz/\n\nn. 花费( expenditure的复数形式 ); 使用; （尤指金钱的）支出额; （精力、时间、材料等的）耗费\n\n释义: n. money paid out; an amount spent\nn. the act of spending money for goods or services\nn. the act of consuming something","color":"3"},{"id":"5542f626d267863b","type":"text","x":610,"y":3410,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"chip\n\nchip\n/tʃip/\n<v:8/n:92>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\n**chip in**: 加入\n\nn. 屑片, 薄片, 碎片\nvt. 削, 切, 削成碎片, 使摔倒, 凿\nvi. 削下屑片\n[计] 孔屑; 组件; 晶片; 芯片\n\n释义: n. a triangular wooden float attached to the end of a log line\nn. a piece of dried bovine dung\nn. a thin crisp slice of potato fried in deep fat\nn. a small disk-shaped counter used to represent money when gambling","color":"1"},{"id":"20201c4a460fcc8d","type":"text","x":50,"y":3550,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"illusion\n\nillusion\n/i'lju:ʒәn/\n<n:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 幻影, 错觉, 幻想\n[医] 错觉\n\n释义: n. an erroneous mental representation\nn. something many people believe that is false","color":"1"},{"id":"32400e6ef7d384c5","type":"text","x":330,"y":3550,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"enthusiasm\n\nenthusiasm\n/in'θju:ziæzәm/\n<n:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 巨大的热情, 热心\n\n释义: n. a feeling of excitement\nn. a lively interest","color":"1"},{"id":"6cb82bbb618a84a0","type":"text","x":610,"y":3550,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"reluctance\n\nreluctance\n/ri'lʌktәns/\n<n:100>\n\nn. 不情愿, 勉强\n[电] 磁阻\n\n释义: n. (physics) opposition to magnetic flux (analogous to electric resistance)\nn. a certain degree of unwillingness","color":"3"},{"id":"8eac0d251f94b01b","type":"text","x":50,"y":3690,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"not least\n\n同样重要的是、尤其是","color":"3"},{"id":"b191dff11a3eac5a","type":"text","x":330,"y":3690,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"By all means\n\n无论如何","color":"3"},{"id":"9b43acb887842d31","type":"text","x":610,"y":3690,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"unrealistic\n\nunrealistic\n/.ʌnriә'listik/\n<j:100>\n\na. 不切实际的, 幻想的\n\n释义: a. not realistic","color":"3"},{"id":"ba25d12323cd3e06","type":"text","x":50,"y":3830,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"deceptive\n\ndeceptive\n/di'septiv/\n<j:100>\n[cet6 toefl]\n\na. 迷惑的, 虚伪的, 欺诈的\n\n释义: s. causing one to believe what is not true or fail to believe what is true\ns. designed to deceive or mislead either deliberately or inadvertently","color":"1"},{"id":"35767aa6ece47f79","type":"text","x":330,"y":3830,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"tiresome\n\ntiresome\n/'taiәsәm/\n<j:100>\n[cet6 ky]\n\na. 累人的, 烦人的\n\n释义: s so lacking in interest as to cause mental weariness","color":"1"},{"id":"68cb3012dda3f6f1","type":"text","x":610,"y":3830,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"nuisance\n\nnuisance\n/'nju:sns/\n<n:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky ielts]\n\nn. 讨厌的东西, 讨厌的人, 损害\n[医] 损害, 讨厌\n\n释义: n. (law) a broad legal concept including anything that disturbs the reasonable use of your property or endangers life and health or is offensive","color":"1"},{"id":"708d31ff631b9b61","type":"text","x":50,"y":3970,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"outperforming\n\noutperforming\n/ˌaʊtpəˈfɔ:mɪŋ/\n\nv. 做得比…更好, 胜过( outperform的现在分词 )\n\n释义: v be or do something to a greater degree","color":"3"},{"id":"09b4fbaf16f14f92","type":"text","x":330,"y":3970,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"reassessing\n\nreassessing\n/ˈri:əˈsesɪŋ/\n\nv. 再估价, 再评价, 再课税( reassess的现在分词 )\n\n释义: v revise or renew one's assessment","color":"3"},{"id":"e0706e7492ec75f7","type":"text","x":610,"y":3970,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"negative\n\nnegative\n/'negәtiv/\n<j:94/n:6>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 否定, 否定语, 负数, 底片\na. 否定的, 消极的, 负的, 阴性的\nn. 负数, 负值\n[计] 负数, 负值\n\n释义: n. a reply of denial\nn. a piece of photographic film showing an image with light and shade or colors reversed\na. characterized by or displaying negation or denial or opposition or resistance; having no positive features\na. expressing or consisting of a negation or refusal or denial","color":"1"},{"id":"dae76efacd810ca7","type":"text","x":50,"y":4110,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"incompetent\n\nincompetent\n/in'kɒmpitәnt/\n<j:96/n:4>\n[toefl gre]\n\na. 无能力的, 无资格的, 机能不全的, 不胜任的\nn. 无能力者\n\n释义: n. someone who is not competent to take effective action\na. legally not qualified or sufficient\na. not qualified or suited for a purpose\ns. not doing a good job","color":"1"},{"id":"8082a09006c753be","type":"text","x":330,"y":4110,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"perceived\n\nperceived\n/pə'siːvd/\n<j:100>\n\nv. 感觉( perceive的过去式和过去分词 ); 视为; 认为; 理解为\n\n释义: s. detected by means of the senses","color":"1"},{"id":"8ae13f8bd7353340","type":"text","x":610,"y":4110,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"disguised\n\ndisguised\n/disˈɡaizd/\n<j:100>\n\nv. 假扮( disguise的过去式和过去分词 ); 化装; 伪装; 掩盖\n\n释义: v make unrecognizable\ns having its true character concealed with the intent of misleading","color":"1"},{"id":"e2d1fae3d98b3a1f","type":"text","x":50,"y":4250,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"bear\n\nbear\n/bєә/\n<n:36/v:64>\n[gk toefl ielts]\n\nn. 熊\nvt. 忍受, 支承, 产生, 怀有, 通过卖空使跌价\nvi. 忍受, 结果实, 压挤, 行进, 转向\n\n释义: n. massive plantigrade carnivorous or omnivorous mammals with long shaggy coats and strong claws\nn. an investor with a pessimistic market outlook; an investor who expects prices to fall and so sells now in order to buy later at a lower price\nv. have\nv. move while holding up or supporting","color":"1"},{"id":"9885113d90b9ea6a","type":"text","x":330,"y":4250,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"coming across\n\n给别人留下某种印象","color":"3"},{"id":"91a7afed69220253","type":"text","x":610,"y":4250,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"tipped\n\ntipped\n\n给小费","color":"3"},{"id":"2f79304f7675c251","type":"text","x":50,"y":4390,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"via\n\nvia\n/vaiә/\n<i:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nprep. 经由, 经过, 通过\n[医] 病毒灭活剂\n\n释义: n. A road way.\nprep. By the way of; as, to send a letter via Queenstown to\n   London.","color":"1"},{"id":"5648ed3a5f18ffda","type":"text","x":330,"y":4390,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"purchases\n\npurchases\n\nv. 购买；进货（purchase的第三人称单数形式）\n\n释义: n the acquisition of something for payment\nn something acquired by purchase\nn a means of exerting influence or gaining advantage\nn the mechanical advantage gained by being in a position to use a lever\nv obtain by purchase; acquire by means of a financial transaction","color":"3"},{"id":"f09f12958ba208c9","type":"text","x":610,"y":4390,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"diligence\n\ndiligence\n/'dilidʒәns/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 gre]\n\nn. 勤奋\n\n释义: n. conscientiousness in paying proper attention to a task; giving the degree of care required in a given situation\nn. persevering determination to perform a task","color":"1"},{"id":"8cb218bd9c496108","type":"text","x":50,"y":4530,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"determine\n\ndetermine\n/di'tә:min/\n<v:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nv. 决定, 决心\n\n释义: v. establish after a calculation, investigation, experiment, survey, or study\nv. shape or influence; give direction to\nv. fix conclusively or authoritatively\nv. fix in scope; fix the boundaries of","color":"1"},{"id":"8e0df54a89626136","type":"text","x":330,"y":4530,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"beforehand\n\nbeforehand\n/bi'fɒ:hænd/\n<r:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nadv. 预先\n\n释义: s being ahead of time or need\nr ahead of time; in anticipation","color":"1"},{"id":"507d32879a05f2bb","type":"text","x":610,"y":4530,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"prevalence\n\nprevalence\n/'prevәlәns/\n<n:100>\n[cet6]\n\nn. 普遍, 流行, 广泛\n[医] 流行, 盛行\n\n释义: n. the quality of prevailing generally; being widespread\nn. (epidemiology) the ratio (for a given time period) of the number of occurrences of a disease or event to the number of units at risk in the population","color":"1"},{"id":"0f8d34d11820734c","type":"text","x":50,"y":4670,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"routinely\n\nroutinely\n<r:100>\n[toefl]\n\nadv. 日常, 乏味, 常规, 例行\n\n释义: r. according to routine or established practice","color":"1"},{"id":"b103f068ca778efe","type":"text","x":330,"y":4670,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"owe\n\nowe\n/әu/\n<v:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky ielts]\n\nvt. 亏欠, 负...债, 归功于, 怀有, 应给予, 感恩\nvi. 欠钱\n\n释义: v. be obliged to pay or repay\nv. be indebted to, in an abstract or intellectual sense\nv. be in debt","color":"3"},{"id":"622154f2bd782845","type":"text","x":610,"y":4670,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"creep\n\ncreep\n/kri:p/\n<n:18/v:82>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 爬, 徐行, 蠕动\nvi. 爬, 蔓延, 潜行\n\n释义: n. someone unpleasantly strange or eccentric\nn. a slow longitudinal movement or deformation\nn. a pen that is fenced so that young animals can enter but adults cannot\nv. grow or spread, often in such a way as to cover (a surface)","color":"1"},{"id":"ea19953d0d782fbe","type":"text","x":50,"y":4810,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"fizzled\n\nfizzled\n/ˈfizld/\n\nv. 发嘶嘶声, 失败( fizzle的过去式和过去分词 )\n\n释义: imp. & p. p. of Fizzle","color":"1"},{"id":"2ff905b4d2a00a45","type":"text","x":330,"y":4810,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"succumbing\n\nsuccumbing\n/səˈkʌmɪŋ/\n\nv. 不再抵抗（诱惑、疾病、攻击等）( succumb的现在分词 ); 屈从; 被压垮; 死\n\n释义: p. pr. & vb. n. of Succumb","color":"3"},{"id":"6045c8d4dd51e242","type":"text","x":610,"y":4810,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"temptations\n\ntemptations\n/tempˈteiʃənz/\n\nn. 诱惑, 引诱( temptation的复数形式 ); 诱惑物\n\n释义: n. something that seduces or has the quality to seduce\nn. the desire to have or do something that you know you should avoid\nn. the act of influencing by exciting hope or desire","color":"3"},{"id":"70814310002bf69e","type":"text","x":50,"y":4950,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"frustrated\n\nfrustrated\n/frʌ'streitid/\n<j:100>\n\na. 失意的, 挫败的；泄气的\n\n释义: v hinder or prevent (the efforts, plans, or desires) of\nv treat cruelly\ns disappointingly unsuccessful","color":"1"},{"id":"ef7bd0e1204e151f","type":"text","x":330,"y":4950,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"coercive\n\ncoercive\n/kәu'ә:siv/\n<j:100>\n\na. 强制的, 强压的, 强迫的\n[法] 强制的, 强迫的, 强行的\n\n释义: s. serving or intended to coerce","color":"3"},{"id":"e1a02f78780a968d","type":"text","x":610,"y":4950,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"dissociated\n\ndissociated\n/dɪ'səʊʃɪeɪtɪd/\n<j:100>\n\na. 解离的\nv. 使分离( dissociate的过去式和过去分词 ); 分离\n\n释义: v part; cease or break association with\nv regard as unconnected\nv to undergo a reversible or temporary breakdown of a molecule into simpler molecules or atoms","color":"3"},{"id":"91696eba262fd17d","type":"text","x":50,"y":5090,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"deficiencies\n\ndeficiencies\n/diˈfiʃənsiz/\n\nn. 缺乏( deficiency的名词复数 ); 不足; 缺点; 缺陷\n\n释义: pl.  of Deficiency","color":"3"},{"id":"dde110a0bd70f6cd","type":"text","x":330,"y":5090,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"barely\n\nbarely\n/'bєәli/\n<r:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nadv. 几乎不\n\n释义: r. only a very short time before","color":"1"},{"id":"aaeb0f7145538d4a","type":"text","x":610,"y":5090,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"rivalled\n\nrivalled\n\n竞争（rival 的过去式和过去分词）\n\n释义:  of Rival","color":"3"},{"id":"57b812039bc7197a","type":"text","x":50,"y":5230,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"rehearsed\n\nrehearsed\n/rɪˈhɜ:st/\n<j:100>\n\nv. 排练, 排演( rehearse的过去式和过去分词 ); 详述\n\n释义: v engage in a rehearsal (of)","color":"3"},{"id":"3811073bc749ae6f","type":"text","x":330,"y":5230,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"burden\n\nburden\n/'bә:dn/\n<v:12/n:88>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nn. 负担, 重载, 担子, 责任\nvt. 装货于, 烦扰, 使负担\n\n释义: n. an onerous or difficult concern\nn. the central idea that is expanded in a document or discourse\nv. weight down with a load","color":"1"},{"id":"0bd1b764c045ad64","type":"text","x":610,"y":5230,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"reinforce\n\nreinforce\n/.ri:in'fɒ:s/\n<v:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nvt. 加强, 增援, 补充\nvi. 求援, 得到增援\nn. 加固材料\n\n释义: v. make stronger\nv. strengthen and support with rewards","color":"1"},{"id":"d8902a5293e84304","type":"text","x":50,"y":5370,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"resume\n\nresume\n/ri'zju:m/\n<n:18/v:82>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nvt. 重新开始, 取回, 恢复\nvi. 再开始\nn. 摘要, 个人简历\n[计] 继续执行\n\n释义: v. take up or begin anew\nv. return to a previous location or condition\nv. assume anew","color":"1"},{"id":"cc50fc6db48f87b6","type":"text","x":330,"y":5370,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"suspended\n\nsuspended\n<j:100>\n\na. 悬浮的；暂停的, 缓期的（宣判）\n\n释义: s. (of undissolved particles in a fluid) supported or kept from sinking or falling by buoyancy and without apparent attachment","color":"1"},{"id":"26d6e32a6ed9dfa2","type":"text","x":610,"y":5370,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"estimated\n\nestimated\n<j:100>\n\na. 估算的；估计的；预计的\n\n释义: v judge tentatively or form an estimate of (quantities or time)\nv judge to be probable","color":"1"},{"id":"033a88126ed90840","type":"text","x":50,"y":5510,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"determinants\n\ndeterminants\n/dɪ'tɜ:mɪnənts/\n\nn. 决定物, 决定因素( determinant的复数形式 )\n\n释义: n. a determining or causal element or factor\nn. the site on the surface of an antigen molecule to which an antibody attaches itself\nn. a square matrix used to solve simultaneous equations","color":"1"},{"id":"72133148bf34b451","type":"text","x":330,"y":5510,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"obesity\n\nobesity\n/әu'bi:siti/\n<n:100>\n\nn. 肥胖\n[医] 肥胖, 多脂\n\n释义: n more than average fatness","color":"3"},{"id":"e2ba9ada4bb5c38a","type":"text","x":610,"y":5510,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"scrapped\n\nscrapped\n<j:100>\n\na. 报废的；已经销毁的\n\n释义: v dispose of (something useless or old)\nv have a disagreement over something\nv make into scrap or refuse","color":"3"},{"id":"f115c8a61c608c35","type":"text","x":50,"y":5650,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"taxpayers\n\ntaxpayers\n/'tækspeɪəz/\n\nn. 纳税人, 纳税的机构( taxpayer的复数形式 )\n\n释义: n. someone who pays taxes","color":"3"},{"id":"e0d4f3ec9f0df09c","type":"text","x":330,"y":5650,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"hefty\n\nhefty\n/'hefti/\n<j:100>\n\na. 重的, 肌肉发达的\n\n释义: s. of considerable weight and size","color":"4"},{"id":"eab4a733bb83a53f","type":"text","x":610,"y":5650,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"proliferating\n\nproliferating\n<j:100>\n\n[医] 增生的\n\n释义: v grow rapidly\nv cause to grow or increase rapidly","color":"3"},{"id":"c488c77c27d0baf4","type":"text","x":50,"y":5790,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"excessive\n\nexcessive\n/ik'sesiv/\n<j:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\na. 过度的, 过多的, 极端的\n[法] 过度的, 过分的, 额外的\n\n释义: s. beyond normal limits\ns. unrestrained, especially with regard to feelings","color":"1"},{"id":"0892e307e5488f34","type":"text","x":330,"y":5790,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"emergency\n\nemergency\n/i'mә:dʒәnsi/\n<j:1/n:99>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky ielts gre]\n\nn. 紧急状况, 紧急事件, 紧急需要\n[化] 紧急情况\n\n释义: n. a sudden unforeseen crisis (usually involving danger) that requires immediate action\nn. a state in which martial law applies","color":"1"},{"id":"d6d1ed7c47752fb1","type":"text","x":610,"y":5790,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"uneven\n\nuneven\n/.ʌn'i:vәn/\n<j:100>\n[ielts]\n\na. 不平坦的, 不均等的, 奇数的\n\n释义: a. not even or uniform as e.g. in shape or texture\ns. variable and recurring at irregular intervals","color":"1"},{"id":"a18c4cd14231b4be","type":"text","x":50,"y":5930,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"thresholds\n\nthresholds\n/θ'reʃhəʊldz/\n\nn. 门槛( threshold的复数形式 ); [物理学]临界值; [英国英语]级限协定; [航空学]跑道入口\n\n释义: n. the starting point for a new state or experience\nn. the smallest detectable sensation\nn. the entrance (the space in a wall) through which you enter or leave a room or building; the space that a door can close","color":"4"},{"id":"af63e462d15af7cd","type":"text","x":330,"y":5930,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"gauge\n\ngauge\n/geidʒ/\n<v:23/n:77>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 标准度量, 计量器\nvt. 精确计量, 估计\n[计] 线规\n\n释义: n. a measuring instrument for measuring and indicating a quantity such as the thickness of wire or the amount of rain etc.\nn. accepted or approved instance or example of a quantity or quality against which others are judged or measured or compared\nn. the distance between the rails of a railway or between the wheels of a train\nn. the thickness of wire","color":"1"},{"id":"be5e19406bffd76e","type":"text","x":610,"y":5930,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"nuanced\n\nnuanced\n/'nju:ɔnst, 'nu:-';nju:'ɔnst/\n<j:100>\n\n(色彩、音调、措词、意味、香韵、感情等)有细微差别的","color":"4"},{"id":"2c128c51098b21b9","type":"text","x":50,"y":6070,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"amplified\n\namplified\n<j:100>\n\nv. 放大；详述（amplify的过去分词）\n\n释义: v increase in size, volume or significance\nv to enlarge beyond bounds or the truth\nv exaggerate or make bigger\nv increase the volume of","color":"3"},{"id":"33e58e6206ca9465","type":"text","x":330,"y":6070,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"humidity\n\nhumidity\n/hju:'miditi/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 湿气, 潮湿, 湿度\n[计] 湿度\n\n释义: n. wetness in the atmosphere","color":"1"},{"id":"8934713b2871c983","type":"text","x":610,"y":6070,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"neglected\n\nneglected\n/ni'^lektid/\n<j:100>\n\na. 被忽视的, 未被好好照管的\n[法] 未被好好照管的, 被忽视的\n\n释义: s. lacking a caretaker","color":"3"},{"id":"cb95032dc09c7fb2","type":"text","x":50,"y":6210,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"ceremony\n\nceremony\n/'serimәni/\n<n:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 典礼, 仪式, 礼节\n[法] 典礼, 仪式\n\n释义: n. a formal event performed on a special occasion\nn. any activity that is performed in an especially solemn elaborate or formal way\nn. the proper or conventional behavior on some solemn occasion","color":"1"},{"id":"0f0189f961cfaf77","type":"text","x":330,"y":6210,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"relief\n\nrelief\n/ri'li:f/\n<n:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 减轻, 解除, 救济, 安慰, 调剂, 浮雕, 换班, (地势的)起伏\n[医] 缓减, 减轻, 浮雕(绘画中)\n\n释义: n. the feeling that comes when something burdensome is removed or reduced\nn. the condition of being comfortable or relieved (especially after being relieved of distress)\nn. (law) redress awarded by a court\nn. assistance in time of difficulty","color":"1"},{"id":"c5287894fa4dc7cc","type":"text","x":610,"y":6210,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"retrofit\n\nretrofit\n/'retrә,fit/\n<n:38/v:62>\n\nn. 式样翻新\nvt.vi. 式样翻新\n[计] 更新; 改进\n\n释义: n. a component or accessory added to something after it has been manufactured\nn. the act of adding a component or accessory to something that did not have it when it was manufactured\nv. provide with parts, devices, or equipment not available or in use at the time of the original manufacture","color":"3"},{"id":"153d850db8d002f2","type":"text","x":50,"y":6350,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"grants\n\ngrants\n[cet6 ielts]\n\n[经] 补助金, 拨款, 津贴\n\n释义: n any monetary aid\nn the act of providing a subsidy\nn (law) a transfer of property by deed of conveyance\nn Scottish painter; cousin of Lytton Strachey and member of the Bloomsbury Group (1885-1978)\nn United States actor (born in England) who was the elegant leading man in many films (1904-1986)\nn 18th President of the United States; commander of the Union armies in the American Civil War (1822-1885)\nn a contract granting the right to operate a subsidiary business\nn a right or privilege that has been granted\nv let have\nv give as judged due or on the basis of merit\nv be willing to concede\nv allow to have\nv bestow, especially officially\nv give over; surrender or relinquish to the physical control of another\nv transfer by deed","color":"1"},{"id":"6ba8be2f4a336f81","type":"text","x":330,"y":6350,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"pavements\n\npavements\n/'peɪvmənts/\n\nn. 人行道( pavement的复数形式 ); 硬路面; 铺过的路面\n\n释义: n. the paved surface of a thoroughfare\nn. material used to pave an area\nn. walk consisting of a paved area for pedestrians; usually beside a street or roadway","color":"4"},{"id":"8d0cc3d697090004","type":"text","x":610,"y":6350,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"collective\n\ncollective\n/kә'leiktiv/\n<j:86/n:14>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\na. 集体的, 聚集的, 共同的\n[医] 集体的, 集合的\n\n释义: n. members of a cooperative enterprise\na. forming a whole or aggregate\ns. set up on the principle of collectivism or ownership and production by the workers involved usually under the supervision of a government","color":"1"},{"id":"78807c6878dd4439","type":"text","x":50,"y":6490,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"preferences\n\npreferences\n\n[计] 参数选择\n\n释义: n a strong liking\nn a predisposition in favor of something\nn the right or chance to choose\nn grant of favor or advantage to one over another (especially to a country or countries in matters of international trade, such as levying duties)","color":"4"},{"id":"0d1d87eef428c48f","type":"text","x":330,"y":6490,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"solitude\n\nsolitude\n/'sɒlitju:d/\n<n:100>\n[ky toefl gre]\n\nn. 孤独, 单独, 孤寂\n\n释义: n. a state of social isolation\nn. the state or situation of being alone\nn. a solitary place","color":"3"},{"id":"1e4cb2248a2b05b3","type":"text","x":610,"y":6490,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"capability\n\ncapability\n/.keipә'biliti/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 toefl]\n\nn. 能力, 性能, 约束力\n[化] 能力\n\n释义: n. the quality of being capable -- physically or intellectually or legally\nn. the susceptibility of something to a particular treatment\nn. an aptitude that may be developed","color":"1"},{"id":"c879cfdc1ddaa111","type":"text","x":50,"y":6630,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"interpret\n\ninterpret\n/in'tә:prit/\n<v:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nvt. 解释, 演出, 翻译, 理解\nvi. 翻译, 解释\n\n释义: v. make sense of; assign a meaning to\nv. give an interpretation or rendition of","color":"1"},{"id":"c5d28763b3b28686","type":"text","x":330,"y":6630,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"lawn\n\nlawn\n/lɒ:n/\n<n:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 草地, 草坪, 上等细麻布\n[机] 细筛\n\n释义: n. a field of cultivated and mowed grass","color":"1"},{"id":"3578cb8f6ba41ad3","type":"text","x":610,"y":6630,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"proceeded\n\nproceeded\n/prəˈsi:did/\n\nv. 进行( proceed的过去式和过去分词 ); 前进; （沿特定路线）行进; （尤指打断后）继续说\n\n释义: imp. & p. p. of Proceed","color":"1"},{"id":"9c98608c34c47f87","type":"text","x":50,"y":6770,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"pave\n\npave\n/peiv/\n<v:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nvt. 铺设, 安排, 铺满, 为...铺路\n[化] 铺设\n\n释义: n. a setting with precious stones so closely set that no metal shows\nv. cover with a material such as stone or concrete to make suitable for vehicle traffic","color":"1"},{"id":"cf42a47f298a513b","type":"text","x":330,"y":6770,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"persists\n\npersists\n/pəˈsists/\n\nv. 坚持( persist的第三人称单数 ); 维持; 保持; 持续存在\n\n释义: v continue to exist\nv be persistent, refuse to stop\nv stay behind","color":"1"},{"id":"f207c71f4d131c5a","type":"text","x":610,"y":6770,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"devote\n\ndevote\n/di'vәut/\n<v:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nvt. 投入于, 献身\n\n释义: v. set aside or apart for a specific purpose or use","color":"1"},{"id":"69d0f95aaa6435ee","type":"text","x":50,"y":6910,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"boast\n\nboast\n/bәust/\n<n:10/v:90>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 吹牛\nvi. 吹牛, 自夸\nvt. 夸口说, 自恃有\n\n释义: n. speaking of yourself in superlatives\nv. show off","color":"1"},{"id":"0158cf2e3cffb469","type":"text","x":330,"y":6910,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"showcases\n\nshowcases\n/ˈʃəʊˌkeɪsiz/\n\nn. （商店或博物馆等的）玻璃柜台, 玻璃陈列柜( showcase的复数形式 ); 展示（本领、才华或优良品质）的场合\nv. （商店或博物馆等的）玻璃柜台, 玻璃陈列柜( showcase的第三人称单数 ); 展示（本领、才华或优良品质）的场合\n\n释义: n. a setting in which something can be displayed to best effect\nn. a glass container used to store and display items in a shop or museum or home","color":"1"},{"id":"352e793b4eb1a13a","type":"text","x":610,"y":6910,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"instruct\n\ninstruct\n/in'strʌkt/\n<v:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nvt. 教, 教育, 命令, 通知\n[法] 托办, 指导, 指示\n\n释义: v. give instructions or directions for some task\nv. make aware of","color":"1"},{"id":"b6ec6f185f1237cb","type":"text","x":50,"y":7050,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"instructing\n\ninstructing\n/inˈstrʌktɪŋ/\n\nv. 教( instruct的现在分词 ); 通知; 教授; 命令\n\n释义: p. pr. & vb. n. of Instruct","color":"1"},{"id":"289d8b0c5db821c2","type":"text","x":330,"y":7050,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"pedestrians\n\npedestrians\n/pɪ'destrɪəns/\n\nn. 步行者( pedestrian的复数形式 )\n\n释义: n. a person who travels by foot","color":"3"},{"id":"2458f739084a256a","type":"text","x":610,"y":7050,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"adhere\n\nadhere\n/әd'hiә/\n<v:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nvi. 依附, 粘着, 坚持, 追随, 拥护\nvt. 使粘附\n\n释义: v. be compatible or in accordance with\nv. follow through or carry out a plan without deviation\nv. be a devoted follower or supporter\nv. stick to firmly","color":"1"},{"id":"e4e555ca54396e72","type":"text","x":50,"y":7190,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"designated\n\ndesignated\n/'deziɡ.neitid/\n<j:100>\n\na. 特指的；指定的\n\n释义: v assign a name or title to\nv give an assignment to (a person) to a post, or assign a task to (a person)\nv indicate a place, direction, person, or thing; either spatially or figuratively\nv decree or designate beforehand\nv design or destine","color":"3"},{"id":"c819b26b0e0565f2","type":"text","x":330,"y":7190,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"underscoring\n\nunderscoring\n/ˌʌndəˈskɔ:ɪŋ/\n\nv. 划线于…下, 强调( underscore的现在分词 )\n\n释义: v give extra weight to (a communication)\nv draw a line or lines underneath to call attention to","color":"3"},{"id":"13a84e5080f5faf7","type":"text","x":610,"y":7190,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"rebellious\n\nrebellious\n/ri'beljәs/\n<j:100>\n[toefl gre]\n\na. 造反的, 反抗的\n[法] 造反的, 反抗的, 反判的\n\n释义: s. resisting control or authority\ns. participating in organized resistance to a constituted government","color":"3"},{"id":"9a0893c321ef32a5","type":"text","x":50,"y":7330,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"inherent\n\ninherent\n/in'hiәrәnt/\n<j:100>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\na. 固有的, 与生俱来的\n[医] 固有的, 生来的\n\n释义: s existing as an essential constituent or characteristic\ns in the nature of something though not readily apparent","color":"1"},{"id":"19d91deed0a4857c","type":"text","x":330,"y":7330,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"clash\n\nclash\n/klæʃ/\n<v:32/n:68>\n[cet6 ky ielts gre]\n\nn. 冲突, 撞击声, 抵触\nvi. 冲突, 抵触\nvt. 使发出撞击声\n[计] 对撞\n\n释义: n. a state of conflict between persons\nn. a state of conflict between colors\nv. be incompatible; be or come into conflict\nv. disagree violently","color":"1"},{"id":"2856da3cd023a9aa","type":"text","x":610,"y":7330,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"recognition\n\nrecognition\n/.rekәg'niʃәn/\n<n:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nn. 赞誉, 认得, 识别, 承认, 认可, 认识\n[电] 认识\n\n释义: n. the state or quality of being recognized or acknowledged\nn. the process of recognizing something or someone by remembering\nn. approval\nn. (biology) the ability of one molecule to attach to another molecule that has a complementary shape","color":"1"},{"id":"cda1bdc0c645f226","type":"text","x":50,"y":7470,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"obsession\n\nobsession\n/әb'seʃәn/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 痴迷，困扰, 困扰人的情绪\n[医] 强迫观念\n\n释义: n. an unhealthy and compulsive preoccupation with something or someone","color":"1"},{"id":"710fb226dd034916","type":"text","x":330,"y":7470,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"insistence\n\ninsistence\n/in'sistәns/\n<n:100>\n[toefl]\n\nn. 坚持, 坚决主张\n\n释义: n. continual and persistent demands\nn. the act of insisting on something","color":"3"},{"id":"11437bc685bac52a","type":"text","x":610,"y":7470,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"embracing\n\nembracing\n/imˈbreisɪŋ/\n<j:47/n:53>\n\nv. 拥抱( embrace的现在分词 ); 包括; 包含; 接受\n\n释义: n the act of clasping another person in the arms (as in greeting or affection)\nv include in scope; include as part of something broader; have as one's sphere or territory\nv squeeze (someone) tightly in your arms, usually with fondness\nv take up the cause, ideology, practice, method, of someone and use it as one's own","color":"3"},{"id":"a18b5e649e611d7f","type":"text","x":50,"y":7610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"communal\n\ncommunal\n/'kɒmjunәl/\n<j:100>\n[toefl gre]\n\na. 公有的, 公社的\n[法] 公共的, 自治体的, 巴黎公社的\n\n释义: s. for or by a group rather than individuals\na. relating to a small administrative district or community","color":"3"},{"id":"0d5d7d19931d6893","type":"text","x":330,"y":7610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"trait\n\ntrait\n/treit/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 特征, 特性, 一笔, 少许\n\n释义: n. a distinguishing feature of your personal nature","color":"1"},{"id":"6bd882121874e110","type":"text","x":610,"y":7610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"coalition\n\ncoalition\n/.kәuә'liʃәn/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 结合体, 结合, 联合\n[经] 联合, 联盟\n\n释义: n. the state of being combined into one body","color":"1"},{"id":"ab01e3ae696d9b47","type":"text","x":50,"y":7750,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"stubborn\n\nstubborn\n/'stʌbәn/\n<j:100>\n[gk cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 顽固的, 不听话的, 执拗的, 棘手的\n\n释义: a. tenaciously unwilling or marked by tenacious unwillingness to yield","color":"1"},{"id":"ebab1f66a76269b9","type":"text","x":330,"y":7750,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"humble\n\nhumble\n/'hʌmbl/\n<j:83/v:17>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 低下的, 谦逊的, 粗陋的\nvt. 使...卑下, 降低...地位, 贬抑\n\n释义: v. cause to be unpretentious\ns. low or inferior in station or quality\na. marked by meekness or modesty; not arrogant or prideful\ns. used of unskilled work (especially domestic work)","color":"1"},{"id":"066f7d978f308788","type":"text","x":610,"y":7750,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"abundance\n\nabundance\n/ә'bʌndәns/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 丰富, 充足, 大量\n[经] 丰富, 充裕\n\n释义: n. the property of a more than adequate quantity or supply\nn. (physics) the ratio of the number of atoms of a specific isotope of an element to the total number of isotopes present\nn. (chemistry) the ratio of the total mass of an element in the earth's crust to the total mass of the earth's crust; expressed as a percentage or in parts per million","color":"1"},{"id":"b6babf6931df2c36","type":"text","x":50,"y":7890,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"deficit\n\ndeficit\n/'defisit/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 赤字, 不足额\n[医] 短缺\n\n释义: n. the property of being an amount by which something is less than expected or required\nn. a deficiency or failure in neurological or mental functioning\nn. (sports) the score by which a team or individual is losing\nn. an excess of liabilities over assets (usually over a certain period)","color":"1"},{"id":"d07a4c050b28cc74","type":"text","x":330,"y":7890,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"drained\n\ndrained\n/dreɪnd/\n\nv. （使）流干, （使）逐渐流走( drain的过去式和过去分词 ); 喝光, 喝干; 使（精力、金钱等）耗尽\n\n释义: a. emptied or exhausted of (as by drawing off e.g. water or other liquid)","color":"4"},{"id":"14e1696ecb31cf34","type":"text","x":610,"y":7890,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"whereas\n\nwhereas\n/hwєәr'æz/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nconj. 然而, 鉴于\n[法] 考虑到, 鉴于, 就...而论\n\n释义: adv. At which place; where.\nconj. Considering that; it being the case that; since; --\n   used to introduce a preamble which is the basis of declarations,\n   affirmations, commands, requests, or like, that follow.\nconj. When in fact; while on the contrary; the case being in\n   truth that; although; -- implying opposition to something that\n   precedes; or implying recognition of facts, sometimes followed by a\n   different statement, and sometimes by inferences or something\n   consequent.","color":"1"},{"id":"3a9ebd883c37538a","type":"text","x":50,"y":8030,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"spoiled\n\nspoiled\n\nspoil的过去式和过去分词\n[经] 损坏的\n\n释义: s. having the character or disposition harmed by pampering or oversolicitous attention","color":"3"},{"id":"a79118144e268adf","type":"text","x":330,"y":8030,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"misguided\n\nmisguided\n/mis'gaidid/\n\na. 被误导的\n\n释义: s. wrong in e.g. opinion or judgment","color":"3"},{"id":"8c8b1939c73ed2d3","type":"text","x":610,"y":8030,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"overwhelming\n\noverwhelming\n/.әuvә'hwelmiŋ/\n[cet6 ky]\n\na. 压倒性的, 无法抵抗的\n\n释义: v overcome, as with emotions or perceptual stimuli\nv charge someone with too many tasks\nv cover completely or make imperceptible\nv overcome by superior force\ns so strong as to be irresistible\ns very intense","color":"1"},{"id":"73425823724e0ba7","type":"text","x":50,"y":8170,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"sport\n\nsport\n/spɒ:t/\n[zk gk ielts gre]\n\nn. 运动, 游戏, 娱乐, 消遣, 玩笑\na. 运动的, 户外穿戴的\nvi. 游戏, 参加体育运动, 戏弄, 产生变种\nvt. 炫耀, 使产生变种\n\n释义: n. an active diversion requiring physical exertion and competition\nn. the occupation of athletes who compete for pay\nn. (Maine colloquial) a temporary summer resident of Maine\nn. a person known for the way she (or he) behaves when teased or defeated or subjected to trying circumstances","color":"3"},{"id":"b89597e3bd3afd17","type":"text","x":330,"y":8170,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"revise\n\nrevise\n/ri'vaiz/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 校订, 修正, 改样\nvt. 校订, 修正, 校正\n\n释义: v. make revisions in","color":"3"},{"id":"3c628c46984e7d13","type":"text","x":610,"y":8170,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"downtime\n\ndowntime\n/'dauntaim/\n\nn. 停工期\n[计] 故障停机时间\n\n释义: n. a period of time when something (as a machine or factory) is not operating (especially as a result of malfunctions)","color":"4"},{"id":"fa48e404e07a8a9f","type":"text","x":50,"y":8310,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"burnout\n\nburnout\n/'bә:naut/\n\nn. 烧尽, 烧坏, 熄火\n[化] 燃尽","color":"4"},{"id":"b3e477e1c7497d34","type":"text","x":330,"y":8310,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"fatigue\n\nfatigue\n/fә'ti:g/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 疲乏, 疲劳\nvt. 使疲劳, 使心智衰弱\nvi. 疲劳\na. 疲劳的\n\n释义: n. temporary loss of strength and energy resulting from hard physical or mental work\nn. used of materials (especially metals) in a weakened state caused by long stress\nn. (always used with a modifier) boredom resulting from overexposure to something","color":"1"},{"id":"eb3d60b6c888ebb9","type":"text","x":610,"y":8310,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"criticism\n\ncriticism\n/'kritisizm/\n[cet4 cet6 ky]\n\nn. 批评, 评论, 非难\n[法] 批判, 批评, 评论\n\n释义: n. disapproval expressed by pointing out faults or shortcomings\nn. a serious examination and judgment of something\nn. a written evaluation of a work of literature","color":"1"},{"id":"3b86529fb66104c9","type":"text","x":50,"y":8450,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"dilemma\n\ndilemma\n/di'lemә/\n[gk cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 困境, (进退两难的)窘境\n\n释义: n. state of uncertainty or perplexity especially as requiring a choice between equally unfavorable options","color":"1"},{"id":"5837ca97f56e5976","type":"text","x":330,"y":8450,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"irritability\n\nirritability\n/.iritә'biliti/\n\nn. 易怒, 刺激物, 兴奋性\n[医] 应激性, 兴奋性, 刺激感受性, 兴奋增盛, 过敏\n\n释义: n. an irritable petulant feeling","color":"3"},{"id":"b5951b3a6f05fed9","type":"text","x":610,"y":8450,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"evenly\n\nevenly\n/'i:vәnli/\n[cet6 toefl]\n\nadv. 平衡地, 平坦地, 平等地\n\n释义: r. in equal amounts or shares; in a balanced or impartial way\nr. in a level and regular way","color":"1"},{"id":"280fdb091cee7102","type":"text","x":50,"y":8590,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"undercut\n\nundercut\n/'ʌndәkʌt/\n[gre]\n\nn. 底切, 牛腰部下侧嫩肉, 下口, 下旋削球\nvt. 廉价出售, 底切, 雕出, 下旋削球\nvi. 切除底部\n\n释义: n. the material removed by a cut made underneath\nn. a notch cut in the trunk of tree in order to determine the direction of its fall\nn. a cut made underneath to remove material\nv. cut away material from the underside of (an object) so as to leave an overhanging portion in relief","color":"3"},{"id":"84cd31526b684ded","type":"text","x":330,"y":8590,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"prosperity\n\nprosperity\n/prɒs'periti/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl gre]\n\nn. 繁荣, 茂盛, 成功\n[经] 繁荣\n\n释义: n. an economic state of growth with rising profits and full employment\nn. the condition of prospering; having good fortune","color":"1"},{"id":"c47032f6413900ac","type":"text","x":610,"y":8590,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"embrace\n\nembrace\n/im'breis/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 拥抱\nvt. 拥抱, 互相拥抱, 包含, 收买\nvi. 拥抱\n\n释义: n. the act of clasping another person in the arms (as in greeting or affection)\nn. the state of taking in or encircling\nn. a close affectionate and protective acceptance\nv. include in scope; include as part of something broader; have as one's sphere or territory","color":"4"},{"id":"b85b0060abc65e80","type":"text","x":50,"y":8730,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"transformative\n\ntransformative\n/træns'fɔ:mәtiv/\n\na. 有改革能力的, 起改造作用的\n\n释义: a. Having power, or a tendency, to transform.","color":"4"},{"id":"bb5b9d497a0ed849","type":"text","x":330,"y":8730,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"incur\n\nincur\n/in'kә:/\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nvt. 招致, 蒙受, 遭遇\n[经] 招致, 蒙受, 担负\n\n释义: v. make oneself subject to; bring upon oneself; become liable to","color":"1"},{"id":"bcef6f3803de016d","type":"text","x":610,"y":8730,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"expenditure\n\nexpenditure\n/ik'spenditʃә/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 开支, 费用, 用光, 消费额\n[经] 支出, 费用, 消费\n\n释义: n money paid out; an amount spent\nn the act of spending money for goods or services\nn the act of consuming something","color":"1"},{"id":"4ff0028c06412ebd","type":"text","x":50,"y":8870,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"tremendous\n\ntremendous\n/tri'mendәs/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 巨大的, 非常的, 可怕的\n\n释义: s extraordinarily large in size or extent or amount or power or degree; that a whole civilization should be dependent on technology\"- Walter Lippman\ns extraordinarily good or great; used especially as intensifiers\ns extreme in degree or extent or amount or impact","color":"1"},{"id":"3ee5fc67fa00a024","type":"text","x":330,"y":8870,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"resentment\n\nresentment\n/ri'zentmәnt/\n[cet6 gre]\n\nn. 怨恨, 愤恨\n\n释义: n. a feeling of deep and bitter anger and ill-will","color":"1"},{"id":"adfb39df3b7f7698","type":"text","x":610,"y":8870,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"simmering\n\nsimmering\n/'sɪmərɪŋ/\n\nv. 炖, 慢煮( simmer的现在分词 ); 充满势将爆发的（怒气等）\n\n释义: n cooking in a liquid that has been brought to a boil\nv boil slowly at low temperature","color":"3"},{"id":"ac6d9ec46ae71118","type":"text","x":50,"y":9010,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"elites\n\nelites\n/eiˈli:ts/\n\nn. <法>精华( elite的复数形式 ); 精锐; 上层集团; （统称）掌权人物\n\n释义: n. a group or class of persons enjoying superior intellectual or social or economic status","color":"3"},{"id":"ebd144f178c1219f","type":"text","x":330,"y":9010,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"prosperous\n\nprosperous\n/'prɒspәrәs/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl gre]\n\na. 成功的, 繁盛的, 幸运的\n[经] 繁荣的, 昌盛的\n\n释义: s in fortunate circumstances financially; moderately rich\ns very lively and profitable\ns marked by peace and prosperity\ns presaging or likely to bring good luck","color":"3"},{"id":"93b9aff4fe5ca61f","type":"text","x":610,"y":9010,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"dominance\n\ndominance\n/'dɔminәns/\n\nn. 优势, 显性, 统治, 控制, 支配\n[计] 控制, 扰势\n\n释义: n. the state that exists when one person or group has power over another\nn. the organic phenomenon in which one of a pair of alleles present in a genotype is expressed in the phenotype and the other allele of the pair is not","color":"4"},{"id":"4db152852bcdbfac","type":"text","x":50,"y":9150,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"disparities\n\ndisparities\n/dɪˈspærɪti:z/\n\nn. 不同( disparity的名词复数 ); 不等; 不一致; 悬殊\n\n释义: pl.  of Disparity","color":"4"},{"id":"e089eb47c99ea1c7","type":"text","x":330,"y":9150,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"soar\n\nsoar\n/sɒ:/\n[cet6 ky ielts gre]\n\nn. 高扬, 翱翔\nvi. 往上飞舞, 高耸, 翱翔\n\n释义: n. the act of rising upward into the air\nv. rise rapidly\nv. fly upwards or high in the sky\nv. go or move upward","color":"1"},{"id":"e63299fed0d601ce","type":"text","x":610,"y":9150,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"regional\n\nregional\n/'ri:dʒәnәl/\n[toefl ielts]\n\na. 地方的, 地域性的\n[医] 区的, 部位的\n\n释义: a. characteristic of a region\ns. related or limited to a particular region","color":"4"},{"id":"2df1c22824c82b46","type":"text","x":50,"y":9290,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"side effects\n\n副作用","color":"4"},{"id":"39911181a1e8918a","type":"text","x":330,"y":9290,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"timber\n\ntimber\n/'timbә/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 木材, 木料\nvt. 用木材建造\n\n释义: n. a beam made of wood\nn. a post made of wood","color":"1"},{"id":"1ebde28db1663126","type":"text","x":610,"y":9290,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"lift\n\nlift\n/lift/\n[zk gk cet4 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 举起, 帮助, 昂扬, 电梯\nvt. 升高, 提高, 鼓舞, 清偿, 空运, 举起, 剽窃\nvi. 升起, 消散, 耸立\n\n释义: n. the act of giving temporary assistance\nn. a wave that lifts the surface of the water or ground\nn. a device worn in a shoe or boot to make the wearer look taller or to correct a shortened leg\nn. one of the layers forming the heel of a shoe or boot","color":"3"},{"id":"754b0835162f0298","type":"text","x":50,"y":9430,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"incentive\n\nincentive\n/in'sentiv/\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 动机\na. 激励的\n\n释义: n. a positive motivational influence","color":"3"},{"id":"3a117433b2a0f219","type":"text","x":330,"y":9430,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"fluctuating\n\nfluctuating\n\nv. 波动（fluctuate的ing形式）\n\n释义: s. having unpredictable ups and downs","color":"3"},{"id":"3bce6ca6fd482ee4","type":"text","x":610,"y":9430,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"Unfavourable\n\nunfavourable\n\na. 不适宜的, 不适应的, 不顺利的, 不好的, 相反的, 不同意的, 令人不快的\n\n释义: a not encouraging or approving or pleasing\na (of winds or weather) tending to hinder or oppose\ns not favorable","color":"3"},{"id":"7ad93275a722a2af","type":"text","x":50,"y":9570,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"decimation\n\ndecimation\n/.desi'meiʃәn/\n\nn. 每十人杀一人, 大批杀害\n\n释义: n. destroying or killing a large part of the population (literally every tenth person as chosen by lot)","color":"4"},{"id":"ba7647361c93aff0","type":"text","x":330,"y":9570,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"encompasses\n\nencompasses\n/enˈkʌmpəsiz/\n\nv. 围绕( encompass的第三人称单数 ); 包围; 包含; 包括\n\n释义: v include in scope; include as part of something broader; have as one's sphere or territory","color":"4"},{"id":"52e89e09ce6409c5","type":"text","x":610,"y":9570,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"hesitation\n\nhesitation\n/.hezi'teiʃәn/\n\nn. 犹豫, 踌躇, 含糊, 口吃, 暂停\n[计] 暂停\n\n释义: n. indecision in speech or action\nn. the act of pausing uncertainly","color":"4"},{"id":"5fe7ae4d6421ef27","type":"text","x":50,"y":9710,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"rural\n\nrural\n/'ruәrәl/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 乡下的, 田园的, 乡村风味的\n[法] 农村的, 乡村的, 有关农业的\n\n释义: a. living in or characteristic of farming or country life\na. of or relating to the countryside as opposed to the city","color":"1"},{"id":"d3c93bd38f353de2","type":"text","x":330,"y":9710,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"Subsidise\n\nsubsidise\n\nvt. 给...补助金, 津贴, 资助\n\n释义: v secure the assistance of by granting a subsidy, as of nations or military forces\nv support through subsidies","color":"3"},{"id":"f2e6105a754a7aee","type":"text","x":610,"y":9710,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"impetus\n\nimpetus\n/'impitәs/\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 动力, 推动力, 动量\n[医] 冲动, 动能, 起始(病)\n\n释义: n a force that moves something along\nn the act of applying force suddenly","color":"1"},{"id":"854256ee87dbd718","type":"text","x":50,"y":9850,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"aspirations\n\naspirations\n\nn. 愿望\n\n释义: n a will to succeed\nn a cherished desire\nn a manner of articulation involving an audible release of breath\nn the act of inhaling; the drawing in of air (or other gases) as in breathing","color":"3"},{"id":"bd5a4a67094429c8","type":"text","x":330,"y":9850,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"convincing\n\nconvincing\n/kәn'vinsiŋ/\n[cet6 toefl]\n\n**也可做现在分词，意思是说服，使别人信服**\n\na. 使人信服的, 有力的, 令人心悦诚服的\n\n释义: a. causing one to believe the truth of something","color":"3"},{"id":"023714885a7439af","type":"text","x":610,"y":9850,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"physicians\n\nphysicians\n/fɪ'zɪʃnz/\n\nn. 医生, 内科医生( physician的复数形式 )\n\n释义: n. a licensed medical practitioner","color":"3"},{"id":"199c80330c96d902","type":"text","x":50,"y":9990,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"impairment\n\nimpairment\n/im'peәmәnt/\n\nn. 削弱, 减少, 损害, 损伤, 危害\n[计] 减损\n\n释义: n. damage that results in a reduction of strength or quality","color":"3"},{"id":"9a392a494480040e","type":"text","x":330,"y":9990,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"privileges\n\nprivileges\n/ˈprivilidʒz/\n\nn. 特权( privilege的名词复数 ); （因财富和社会地位而仅有部分人享有的）权益; 免责特权; 特殊荣幸\n\n释义: n a special advantage or immunity or benefit not enjoyed by all\nn a right reserved exclusively by a particular person or group (especially a hereditary or official right)\nn (law) the right to refuse to divulge information obtained in a confidential relationship\nv bestow a privilege upon","color":"3"},{"id":"c9b9c50c32a29d9b","type":"text","x":610,"y":9990,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"ethical\n\nethical\n/'eθikәl/\n[cet6]\n\na. 伦理的, 民族的, 民族特有的\n[医] 伦理的, 道德的\n\n释义: a. of or relating to the philosophical study of ethics\na. conforming to accepted standards of social or professional behavior\ns. adhering to ethical and moral principles","color":"1"},{"id":"815022cca8b3e389","type":"text","x":50,"y":10130,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"substantial\n\nsubstantial\n/sәb'stænʃәl/\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 重要材料(或事物), 有实际价值的东西\na. 实质上的, 物质的, 有内容的, 结实的\n\n释义: s. having a firm basis in reality and being therefore important, meaningful, or considerable\na. having substance or capable of being treated as fact; not imaginary","color":"1"},{"id":"0cfc5f3d6281493e","type":"text","x":330,"y":10130,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"breach\n\nbreach\n/bri:tʃ/\n[ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 裂口, 违背, 破坏, 违反, 突破, 破裂\nvt. 攻破, 突破\nvi. 跳出水面\n\n释义: n. a failure to perform some promised act or obligation\nn. an opening (especially a gap in a dike or fortification)","color":"3"},{"id":"b6f4ddb52801792b","type":"text","x":610,"y":10130,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"liability\n\nliability\n/laiә'biliti/\n[cet6 ky ielts gre]\n\nn. 责任, 债务, 倾向\n[经] 责任, 义务, 负债\n\n释义: n. the state of being legally obliged and responsible\nn. the quality of being something that holds you back","color":"1"},{"id":"da35323e80950a6b","type":"text","x":50,"y":10270,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"penalties\n\npenalties\n/ˈpenəltiz/\n\nn. 惩罚( penalty的名词复数 ); 刑罚; 害处; 足球点球\n\n释义: pl.  of Penalty","color":"4"},{"id":"d12d4d3d5f4e3375","type":"text","x":330,"y":10270,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"in accordance with\n\n根据，依据，和...步调一致","color":"3"},{"id":"08884ae5127344dd","type":"text","x":610,"y":10270,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"confidentiality\n\nconfidentiality\n\n[计] 机密性\n[经] 保密\n\n释义: n. the state of being secret\nn. discretion in keeping secret information","color":"3"},{"id":"17f00a5368022cf5","type":"text","x":50,"y":10410,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"counsel\n\ncounsel\n/'kaunsәl/\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 商议, 忠告, 法律顾问\nv. 商议, 劝告\n\n释义: n a lawyer who pleads cases in court\nn something that provides direction or advice as to a decision or course of action\nv give advice to","color":"1"},{"id":"5a7ff2535c9c0668","type":"text","x":330,"y":10410,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"counseled\n\ncounseled\n\nvt. 劝告, 建议（counsel的过去式与过去分词形式）\n\n释义: imp. & p. p. of Counsel","color":"1"},{"id":"ddc39a2d92f24d41","type":"text","x":610,"y":10410,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"piecemeal\n\npiecemeal\n/'pi:smi:l/\n[ielts gre]\n\nadv. 一件一件地, 逐个地, 零碎地\na. 一片一片的, 逐渐的, 零碎的\nn. 断片\n\n释义: r. a little bit at a time","color":"3"},{"id":"f3819f27e704d068","type":"text","x":50,"y":10550,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"coordinated\n\ncoordinated\n[toefl]\n\nvt. 调节；调整；整理；使调和（coordinate的过去分词）\n\n释义: s. operating as a unit\ns. being dexterous in the use of more than one set of muscle movements\ns. intentionally matched","color":"3"},{"id":"918b773cf65d89c9","type":"text","x":330,"y":10550,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"chronic\n\nchronic\n/'krɒnik/\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 慢性的, 习惯性的\nn. 慢性病患者\n\n释义: a. being long-lasting and recurrent or characterized by long suffering\ns. of long duration\ns. habitual","color":"1"},{"id":"e49b1343adf6dac2","type":"text","x":610,"y":10550,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"anticipated\n\nanticipated\n\na. 预期的；期望的\n\n释义: s. expected hopefully","color":"3"},{"id":"34d272f624f543e2","type":"text","x":50,"y":10690,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"enforcement\n\nenforcement\n/in'fɒ:smәnt/\n\nn. 执行, 强制\n[法] 实施, 加强, 厉行\n\n释义: n. the act of enforcing; ensuring observance of or obedience to","color":"3"},{"id":"f3131cf4bc031fa0","type":"text","x":330,"y":10690,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"fertility\n\nfertility\n/fә'tiliti/\n\nn. 肥沃, 丰饶, 生产力\n[医] 生育力\n\n释义: n. the state of being fertile; capable of producing offspring","color":"3"},{"id":"e0416354e6a66798","type":"text","x":610,"y":10690,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"affirmative\n\naffirmative\n/ә'fә:mәtiv/\n\na. 肯定的, 赞成的, 积极的\nn. 肯定语\n\n释义: n. a reply of affirmation\na. affirming or giving assent\ns. expecting the best","color":"3"},{"id":"a12e41cb440a3bee","type":"text","x":50,"y":10830,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"consent\n\nconsent\n/kәn'sent/\n[cet4 cet6 ky ielts gre]\n\nn. 同意, 许可\nvi. 同意, 赞同\n\n释义: n. permission to do something","color":"1"},{"id":"6e64a28cffe903e5","type":"text","x":330,"y":10830,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"instant\n\ninstant\n/'instәnt/\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nn. 立即, 瞬间\na. 紧急的, 立即的, 即时的\n\n释义: s. in or of the present month","color":"1"}],"edges":[]}